# The front door is the website; every other path is the app (it routes itself).
# "200!" forces the rule even though index.html (the app) exists at "/" — without it Netlify serves the app there.
# "Start free" on the site opens /welcome/door; the installed app opens /today (manifest start_url).
# /es is the Spanish website (site-es.html, built by atlas/mock/build.mjs --lang es); it must sit above the catch-all.
/     /site.html    200!
/es   /site-es.html 200
/*    /index.html   200
